# {{pascalCase project.name}}

A small, standalone Angular application with a page-first structure, signal-based UI state, SCSS styles, and a development proxy for the Spring Boot API.

## Requirements

- Node.js 22.22.3 or later in the 22.x line, 24.15.0 or later in the 24.x line, or 26.0.0 or later in the 26.x line
- npm

## Start developing

```bash
npm install
npm start
```

The frontend is served at `http://localhost:4200`. Requests under `/api` are proxied to the backend at `http://localhost:8080`.

## Build

```bash
npm run build
```

The production build is written to `dist/{{kebabCase project.name}}/browser`.

## Structure

```text
src/app/
  api/                 Generated OpenAPI client and client documentation
  core/                Application-wide providers and infrastructure
  directives/          Reusable attribute and structural directives
  guards/              Route guards
  interceptors/        HTTP interceptors
  layout/              Application shell and layout components
  models/              API and domain models
  pages/               Route-level pages
  services/            HTTP and application services
  shared/              Reusable components, pipes, and utilities
  app.component.ts     Root component
  app.config.ts        Application providers
  app.routes.ts        Lazy-loaded routes
```

Angular components are standalone. The app uses Angular signals and built-in `@if` / `@for` template control flow. Angular 22 enables zoneless change detection by default.

## API client

The typed client in `src/app/api/generated/` is generated from the backend
OpenAPI contract. Keep the backend running and run this from the workspace root:

```bash
cleanstack openapi --input http://localhost:8080/v3/api-docs
```

Or point the command at a saved document:

```bash
cleanstack openapi --input openapi/openapi.json
```

CleanStack regenerates the client safely and keeps files it did not generate.
See `src/app/api/README.md` for details.

{{#unless (eq project.options.auth "none")}}
## Authentication

The app ships with a login page at `/login`, a profile page at `/profile`, a route
guard, and an HTTP interceptor. All application routes are protected by the guard;
anonymous visitors are redirected to the login page and returned to their original
route after signing in.

{{#if (eq project.options.auth "jwt")}}
This project uses JWT bearer tokens. Paste an access token issued by your identity
provider into the login page. The token is stored in `localStorage` under
`cleanstack.access-token` and sent as an `Authorization: Bearer` header to the API.

Token login is intended for local development. For a production browser flow,
regenerate with `--auth oidc`, `--auth keycloak`, or `--auth auth0`.
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq project.options.auth "session")}}
This project uses cookie-based sessions. Sign in with the starter account
`demo` / `demo`; override it with `APP_SECURITY_USERNAME` and `APP_SECURITY_PASSWORD`
in the backend. The login form posts to `/api/auth/login`, Spring Security stores
the session in the `JSESSIONID` cookie, and the interceptor sends that cookie with
API requests.

The login page fetches a CSRF token from `/api/auth/csrf`. Angular's HTTP client
automatically sends the `XSRF-TOKEN` cookie value as the `X-XSRF-TOKEN` header on
state-changing requests.
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq project.options.auth "keycloak")}}
This project uses Keycloak with the OIDC authorization-code flow and PKCE. Set the
issuer and client ID in `src/environments/environment.ts`. Create a public
`cleanstack-ui` client in Keycloak with the redirect URI `http://localhost:4200/login`
and post-logout redirect URI `http://localhost:4200/login`, then enable the standard
flow plus PKCE.
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq project.options.auth "auth0")}}
This project uses Auth0 with the OIDC authorization-code flow and PKCE. Replace the
placeholder issuer and client ID in `src/environments/environment.ts`, then add
`http://localhost:4200/login` as an allowed callback and logout URL for an Auth0
Single Page Application.
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq project.options.auth "oidc")}}
This project uses a generic OIDC provider with the authorization-code flow and PKCE.
Set the issuer, client ID, and scope in `src/environments/environment.ts`, then
register `http://localhost:4200/login` as a redirect URI with your provider.
{{/if}}

{{#if (eq project.options.auth "session")}}
The backend keeps users in an in-memory store by default. Replace it with a
database-backed `UserDetailsService` before production. The actuator health and
OpenAPI endpoints stay public.
{{else}}
The backend validates bearer tokens against the issuer configured in
`src/main/resources/application.yml`. The actuator health and OpenAPI endpoints stay
public.
{{/if}}
{{/unless}}

